WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
All right.

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.690
By popular demand, I'm going to do a sort
of full review of the Andrew Cuomo covid cover

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:12.900
up claims that are circulating so we can try
to sort of sort out what's truth and what's

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.130
lies and what we know about and what we don't
know about and sort of what's relevant to

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:24.130
policy versus what are sort of like the more
a personal scandals in which Andrew Cuomo

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.000
is now embroiled.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.000
So let's get right into it.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.649
Earlier in the pandemic, New York Democratic
Governor Andrew Cuomo was seen as sort of

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:36.590
a model governor in responding to the pandemic.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:42.980
And despite New York being hit very hard,
early, believed to be because of the number

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:48.449
of nonstop flights both to China, sort of
like source one for the virus and Italy and

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:54.050
surrounding parts of Europe, sort of like
source two for the virus in the United States.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:59.390
Despite that, the idea was that Cuomo handled
the virus as well as was possible, given what

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:04.989
we knew at the time and ramped up testing
relatively quickly, as quickly as feasible,

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:09.300
put in place guidelines did shut downs as
necessary.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:16.190
And while much of the United States had three
spikes, New York was able to completely suppress

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:21.710
the what was typically spike to for much of
the country in the middle of the summer.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:26.800
And they had basically the initial spike and
then the false spike, limiting themselves

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.280
to two spikes rather than three.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.670
Thanks to Andrew Cuomo, great work.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:39.210
Now, until more recently, some very serious
allegations of the covering up of deaths have

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.210
surfaced.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.240
So let's go through the allegations.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.070
From the emails I've gotten, a lot of people
don't actually understand what is even being

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.070
alleged.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:52.840
Now, I want to be up front that much of much
of this is still disputed and contested.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:02:00.170
And just about every report has some detail
that is not at least yet confirmed.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.840
But we're going to do the best we can to pass
through the evidence.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:11.459
We have the big scandal and the big allegation
is that at Andrew Cuomo, either direction

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:19.159
or indifference nursing home covid deaths
were undercounted by the state, allegedly

00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:23.500
to the tune of thousands of nursing home covid
deaths.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:29.749
And indeed, the New York Health Department
has made public data that added more than

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:36.209
3800 nursing home deaths to their tally after
this story broke.

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:41.299
And the state now acknowledges that they upped
nursing home deaths by about 40 percent.

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:46.459
Now, it's really important to be clear here,
and this is what a lot of people may be missing.

00:02:46.459 --> 00:02:52.909
This is not an allegation that New York undercounted
covid deaths nationally, even globally.

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:57.560
We believe that there have been far more covid
deaths than the official numbers because of

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.079
people who died, including at home, and were
never tested.

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:08.629
But the allegation is not that the full public
number of New York covid deaths is being artificially

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:13.200
suppressed any more than just were probably
undercounting covid deaths at a global level.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.349
The current New York covid death toll is about
47000 and that has nothing to do with these

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:20.349
allegations.

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:23.980
What's at issue is how many nursing home residents
died.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:29.099
And our best understanding of the undercount
is that there were thousands of nursing home

00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:35.489
residents who became so sick that they went
to a hospital, died in the hospital, and they

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:38.019
were not counted as nursing home deaths.

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:42.450
Now, in a literal sense, they did die at the
hospital.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:47.680
But we all understand that if you are a nursing
home resident who catches the virus at a nursing

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.489
home, you should be counted as a nursing home
death.

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:56.590
From the standpoint of evaluating how well
did Andrew Cuomo protect nursing home residents?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.459
And that's the crux of this.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:02.639
Even if the total number of deaths is not
being lied about, if you undercount nursing

00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:07.459
home deaths, you are making it seem as though
you are much better protecting nursing homes

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:08.809
than you really are.

00:04:08.809 --> 00:04:13.260
So this is dishonest and Andrew Cuomo has
to be held accountable.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.730
This has a real impact.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.419
It's not just academic.

00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:24.319
It's not just a number of families make decisions
about facilities for loved ones, in part based

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:28.800
on whether they believe their loved ones will
or won't be safe at nursing homes.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.440
If you falsely believe that there are way
fewer nursing home covid deaths than there

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.060
really are, you might make a decision about
a loved one based on those deceptive statistics.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.949
So this is very real, very serious, and it
has a real world impact.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.229
Now, what are the defenses?

00:04:45.229 --> 00:04:50.660
The defenses are what we heard from Health
Commissioner Howard Zucker from New York,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:58.300
which is that the state website had always
been clear that deaths it listed for nursing

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.300
homes did.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:04.020
Not include deaths that took place outside
the facility and that the total number of

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.960
deaths was never undercounted.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:09.290
That's the defense from the New York Health
Health Department.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:14.810
Then there's the second piece of this, which
is the criticism that New York State sent

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:20.659
nursing home residents who were hospitalized
back to nursing homes in cases where they

00:05:20.659 --> 00:05:22.659
shouldn't have been sent back.

00:05:22.659 --> 00:05:24.720
This one is more nebulous right now.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.441
We're still learning and learning more about
it.

00:05:26.441 --> 00:05:31.539
Andrew Cuomo is defending this and saying
that everybody that was sent back was sent

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:38.199
back in adherence to in compliance with federal
guidelines and that they didn't do anything

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:39.199
that was wrong.

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:43.990
Now, on the second issue, I'm not really able
to put together a definitive take on it.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.340
We just need more information about that.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:51.000
Now, separately, and this is a lot of stuff
happening all at once to Andrew Cuomo separately,

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.810
there are allegations of Andrew Cuomo being
basically a bad guy, bullying employees and

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.920
treating employees terribly.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.010
I see this as important, but secondary to
the covid scandal.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:06.810
It's a lot of he said she said I can't possibly
analyze it in any serious way other than to

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:12.170
say all of the allegations should be investigated
and the cards should fall where they may.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.660
I don't care that Andrew Cuomo is a Democrat.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:19.150
Whatever whatever is uncovered should be what
it is and it should be dealt with.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:26.000
And then lastly, there are also now new allegations
of inappropriate sexual advances and conduct

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.460
by Andrew Cuomo.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:33.810
Lindsay Boylan, who worked for Cuomo as an
aide, says that on a private jet, Cuomo suggested

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.810
playing strip poker, which made her feel uncomfortable.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.760
Boylan says that that happened after she was
promoted to be Cuomo deputy secretary for

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:46.349
economic development and a special adviser
to him.

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:49.669
She said she initially turned the job down
because she didn't want to be near him, ultimately

00:06:49.669 --> 00:06:50.699
accepted it.

00:06:50.699 --> 00:06:55.660
Boylen also is describing an incident where
they were in his office in New York City on

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.080
Third Avenue.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.850
And when she got up to leave and walk out
a door that Andrew Cuomo allegedly stepped

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.460
in front of her, kissed her on the lips, and
that she was shocked but just kept walking

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.460
out.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:13.729
Now, this is totally separate and this allegation
has to be taken seriously and fully pursued.

00:07:13.729 --> 00:07:14.889
So that's the story.

00:07:14.889 --> 00:07:19.490
As I understand it, some of the emails I received
were implying I wasn't going to talk about

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.400
this because Cuomo is a Democrat.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.719
First of all, we talked about this last week
for a while on the bonus show.

00:07:24.719 --> 00:07:29.120
Secondly, I've said a million times, I don't
care about these politicians beyond.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.689
They're doing things for the people.

00:07:30.689 --> 00:07:33.860
I don't care if they're Democrats or Republicans.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.229
I never defended, you know, Anthony Weiner.

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:38.110
I don't defy politicians.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.810
They all have good and bad.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:43.690
And why wouldn't I talk about Andrew Cuomo,
investigate every single thing?

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:48.090
If the people of New York want him to resign,
he should consider resignation.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:51.719
If there are criminal wrongdoings, then investigate
and prosecute.

00:07:51.719 --> 00:07:55.069
We don't ignore stories because it's a Democrat
on this show.

00:07:55.069 --> 00:07:56.099
That is the full story.

00:07:56.099 --> 00:07:57.110
As far as I understand.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.310
It's a really sort of like four stories.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:05.310
The undercount of nursing home deaths, sending
patients from hospitals back to nursing homes,

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:09.919
the bullying of employees and the alleged
sexual harassment of Lindsay Boyland.

00:08:09.919 --> 00:08:10.919
Those are the four stories.

00:08:10.919 --> 00:08:12.229
As I understand them.

00:08:12.229 --> 00:08:14.229
They are separate stories.

00:08:14.229 --> 00:08:19.729
We could sort of group them as the two covid
stories and the two bullying and harassment

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:20.729
stories.

00:08:20.729 --> 00:10:07.490
And we'll just have to follow all of them
and see where the cards fall.

